WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
[DIGITAL EFFECTS]

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.860
PROFESSOR: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.660
So we'll start a
new chapter now,

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.760
QCD or quantum chromodynamics.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.790
And then, this first
lecture of this chapter, we

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.170
talk about the
production of hadrons.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.170
This is really meant as
an introductory lecture,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.060
but we will also
already see some very

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.970
interesting and useful concepts.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.080
So we want to produce
quarks and anti-quark pairs,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.110
and we do this
electron-positron collisions.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:46.180
We have studied in detail this
first part of the diagram.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.690
Specifically, we
calculated a cross-section

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.820
of muon and
anti-muon production,

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.920
and we also have
seen more changes

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.930
than we have same
kind of particle

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:58.990
in the final state of the
electron-positron scattering

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.700
to electron-positrons.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.730
So now, we've replaced
the muons with our quarks

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.620
and anti-quark pairs.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.500
And the first step, we
want to remind ourselves

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.120
of the available quarks
in this discussion.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.840
So we have the up quark, the
down quark, charm, strange,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.400
top, and bottom.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.230
You see that the
charges are given here,

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.980
and the photon
couples to the charge.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:23.060
So the charge is not 1, but
it's either 2/3 or minus 1/3.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.740
Third

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.110
We have also here
in the table mass

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:29.420
is given for those particles.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:37.780
They range from a few MeV to
173 GeV for the top quark.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.710
The bottom quark is
about 5 GeV heavy.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.520
Remember, when we
discussed re-normalization,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.380
we discussed that those masses
are not fixed parameters,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.080
but in our perturbation
series, they

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.760
run like the [INAUDIBLE] one.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.680
So that might cause some
difficulties later on.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.210
OK so now we want to
produce an up quark

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.835
and an anti-up quark
in this collision.

00:02:00.835 --> 00:02:02.300
So what happens?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.910
So we now have
collisions, and then we

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.370
produce those particles.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.750
So let's say an up quark,
and an anti-up here, and then

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.390
your plus and minus collision.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.390
Those quarks only live
for a very short time,

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.520
or travel a very short
distance in space--

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.680
about 10 to the minus 15 meters.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.410
And then, they
start to pull in out

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.850
of the vacuum gluons, and
quarks, and anti-quark pairs,

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:31.700
and those then form into the
actual hadrons after some time.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.070
And those two pictures here
will look very much the same.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.160
The difference is
the way we treat

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.640
the hadronization-- the actual
fact of forming hadrons.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.800
In this first picture,
we are thinking

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.670
about clustering energy
particles together

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.980
and that way form hadrons.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.770
In this picture here, we connect
them with so-called strings.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.910
And those are two different
ways to model and model

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.040
the production of hadrons.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.060
Remember, when we look
at this process here,

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.400
we are looking at
very low-energy kind

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.480
of or lower-energy
kind of phenomena,

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:13.100
and at lower energies,
the strength of the strong

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.890
interaction, the
strength of QCD, is--

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.480
the coupling is
on the order of 1.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.710
It can be larger than 1.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.970
So perturbation theory
is not possible.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.210
That's why we need
specific models.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.200
This is all I want
to say at this point.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.860
We'll come back to this
discussion later on.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.700
What I actually want to discuss
is what we can learn out

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.900
of measuring cross-section
of hadron production--

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.930
for example, by comparing
directly the cross-section

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:44.280
of [INAUDIBLE] production
with a cross-section we just

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.400
calculated for
muon/anti-muon production.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.320
And experimental
results are given here.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.680
So you see as a
function of energy,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.970
here from 1 GeV to 7 GeV
center of mass energy,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.160
and then the lower
plot just continuing

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.710
from about 10 to 60 GeV.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.960
What you see here is that
there is a rich structure.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.320
So you see those
resonances here,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.130
and you also see that there
seem to be some sort of increase

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:15.140
in the value of this ratio.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.500
So how can we now
understand this?

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.649
At leading order, we
can just write this down

00:04:20.649 --> 00:04:22.360
we just calculate
its cross-section

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.960
for electron-muon scattering,
or for electron-muon production.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.690
And we can write this
very same cross-section

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:35.920
of the leading order for
quark-antiquark production.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:40.210
What we find as differences
is the coupling,

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.710
the coupling itself.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.260
Here, we have to use
the charge of the quarks

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.310
and not the charge
of the electron.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:49.840
So there is an additional
factor here, 1/3 or 2/3 squared.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:54.710
And then, there's the number
of possible quark pairs

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.930
which are available,
and that depends

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.280
on the number of colors.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.250
Remember, each quark appears
with three different colors,

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.610
so we have to account
for this factor.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.500
All right, and then
we built the ratio.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.320
And the ratio, everything
just cancels out--

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.210
great.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.830
So we have just a
number of colors

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.570
times the sum of
the charges squared

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.960
of the quarks available.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.120
What do I mean by "the
quarks available?"

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.830
As we go from lower-energies
to higher energies in this plot

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.720
here, the kinematic--

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.180
the energy is sufficient
to produce particles

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.030
based on the masses available.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.850
So we find that this
explains a step function.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.500
Let's look at a
specific example.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:44.080
So if you look at center
of mass energies, which

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.590
are larger than 2 times the
mass of the bottom quark,

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.620
and maybe lower than 2 times
the mass of the top quark,

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.780
we are in this
specific regime here.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.850
Can you see, this
is almost flat,

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:59.610
and the number we
get is almost 4, OK?

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:02.520
What we get from this
leading order calculation

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:12.100
is 3 times 4 over 9 for our
up quark, 1 over 9 for down,

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:18.250
1 over 9 for strange, 4 over
9 for charm, and 1 over 9

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.990
for our bottom quark, OK?

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:23.560
So we built the sum here
for all quarks which

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:29.340
are kinematically available, and
as an answer, we get 11 over 3.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.970
So this is in very
good agreement--

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.710
a leading order,
very good agreement

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.360
with the experimental results.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.480
11 over 3 is almost 4.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.120
Excellent, so this
is clear indication,

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.560
experimental indication,
that this color factor here

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.030
is a real thing.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:51.510
There seemed to be 3 up quarks,
3 down quarks, 3 charm quarks,

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.310
and so on.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.380
And we also see that
this leading order effect

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.970
here, the leading
order calculation,

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.920
is already very precise.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:04.380
And the reason for this
is that this process here

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.790
is a QED process.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.080
So the production
cross-section is QED process,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.990
as we just discussed.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.080
So now, why do I actually
have this as part

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.420
of our QCD introduction?

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:21.070
First, you learned about
the color factor here, OK?

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:24.010
And second, there is,
indeed, corrections,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.140
and one of the
correction is the one

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:30.190
where you actually produce a
real gluon in the final state.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.790
And those corrections
can be calculated.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.000
If you go to higher order,
you get a correction

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.900
from this radiated gluon.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.450
You also get corrections
which looks like this--

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.070
vertex corrections--
and you find

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:51.000
that the correction here to
[? r ?] is about 1 plus alpha

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.250
s at a specific scale over pi.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:59.520
Now, at a reasonable scale,
this is then about 0.1 the value

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.640
of alpha s, and
pi is 3.14, and so

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:09.640
you get about a few percent, 3%
correction to the r value rate.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:12.460
Why is it so important when
there's a small correction?

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.070
It's a percent or few
percent level correction.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:18.370
What is really important
is that this process can

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:23.590
be used in order to demonstrate
the existence of gluons,

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.050
and so gluons have been
discovered this way.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:30.730
And the way this was done is
by producing the plus and minus

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:35.650
collisions and detecting
three bunches of particles--

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.309
too from the quarks,
and one from the gluons.

00:08:39.309 --> 00:08:42.130
And then, to identify
that this gluon on here

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.400
is actually a gluon and
not some other particle,

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.290
one can look at
angular distributions.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.595
One can identify that this is
a spin 1 particle, and so on.

00:08:50.595 --> 00:08:51.970
So there's a little
bit more work

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.000
needed beyond just showing
that there's [INAUDIBLE],,

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.490
but identifying this
kind of topology

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:01.060
in the plus and minus conditions
led to the discovery of gluons

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.080
in this kind of conditions.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.270
So that was my introduction.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:09.370
As a next step, I want to
add one more step of, now,

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:11.620
how can we learn about
this kind of structures

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.220
before we then dive
into Feinmann diagrams,

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:18.900
or Feinmann calculations,
Feinmann rules for QCD.

